<section class="mp-card mt-3" aria-labelledby="mp-rules-heading">
    <div class="mp-eyebrow">Proposed criteria · not an approved selection policy</div>
    <h2 id="mp-rules-heading" class="mt-2">Activity and evidence are different.</h2>
    <p class="mp-subtle">The leaderboard includes valid saved scored profiles with at least one direct singles result in the last 24 calendar months, including the cutoff date. Low-confidence and provisional estimates are included with their cautions. Older inactive and unrated profiles remain in the directory.</p>
    <h3>Proposed established-evidence label</h3>
    <p class="mp-subtle">This separate label requires all of the following, with match, event and opponent counts measured over 365 days, plus a connected trial reference. It describes evidence maturity, not guaranteed accuracy or permission to appear on the leaderboard.</p>
    <div class="mp-rules"><div><strong>8 singles matches</strong>Recorded direct results</div><div><strong>2 different events</strong>Evidence beyond one weekend</div><div><strong>4 distinct opponents</strong>A varied set of comparisons</div><div><strong>Played within 90 days</strong>Recent activity</div></div>
    <p class="mp-subtle mt-3 mb-0">Membership would never improve a rating or bypass these criteria. Separate age groups and disconnected comparison groups cannot be ranked together.</p>
    <p class="mp-subtle mt-2 mb-0">Preview positions use recorded cohort labels; current-season age eligibility and official selection are not established here.</p>
    <p class="mp-subtle mt-2 mb-0">U10 ball type and court size are not verified by these cohort labels. Do not assume that recorded formats are compatible.</p>
    <p class="mp-subtle mt-2 mb-0">The separate profile-update badge uses the recorded profile update date and a six-calendar-month window. It is informational only: it does not verify identity or exclude a player.</p>
</section>
